 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and roles
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` with every request. A missing or unknown key
+returns 401 (`unauthorized`). A recognized key with insufficient permission
+returns 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+- `viewer` can use every GET route except `/audit`.
+- `cook` has viewer access and can use `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` can use every route.
+
+## Audit
+
+`GET /audit` returns successful write requests in newest-first order. Each
+entry has an ISO 8601 `time`, the caller's `keyName`, the HTTP `method`,
+the URL `path` without its query string, and the response `status`.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
